.github/**

# The real stack parameters, which hold a GitHub personal access token with repo scope.
# parameters.example.json is the tracked template; copy it to parameters.json and fill that
# in. The README used to tell the reader to put a real token in a file that was itself
# tracked, and to remember not to commit it. Making the ignored filename the one the
# instructions use means forgetting is no longer enough to leak a token.
parameters.json

# Never commit credentials, keys or private material. Kept in step with the list the
# pre-commit secret scan enforces.
*.log
secrets/
credentials*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.aws/
node_modules/
*.sqlite
*.db
